---

## Features

| Module | Capabilities |
|---|---|
| `auth` | Static bearer token, OAuth2 client credentials with auto-refresh |
| `datasets` | Create/read/delete datasets, branches, transactions, file upload/download |
| `catalog` | Browse resource tree, search resources, manage folders |
| `ontology` | List object types, query/search objects, apply actions, execute queries |
| `compass` | Upload/download files, list with prefix filter, file metadata |
| `cli` | `palantir-foundry` CLI for datasets, catalog, and ontology operations |

### Resilience built-in

- Automatic retry on `500/502/503/504` with exponential back-off (via `urllib3.Retry`)
- Auto-pagination on all list endpoints
- Structured exception hierarchy mapped from HTTP status codes

---

## Installation

```bash
pip install palantir-foundry
```

Or install from source:

```bash
git clone https://github.com/palantir/foundry-platform-python
cd foundry-platform-python
pip install -e ".[dev]"
```

---

## Quick Start

```python
from palantir_foundry import FoundryClient

client = FoundryClient(
    hostname="https://my-foundry.example.com",
    token="my-api-token",           # from the Foundry Developer Console
)

# Get a dataset
ds = client.datasets.get("ri.foundry.main.dataset.abc123")
print(ds.name, ds.rid)

# List files on the master branch
for f in client.datasets.list_files(ds.rid, branch="master"):
    print(f.path, f.size_bytes)
```

---

## Authentication

### Static bearer token

```python
from palantir_foundry import FoundryClient

client = FoundryClient(
    hostname="https://my-foundry.example.com",
    token="eyJhbGci...",
)
```

### OAuth2 client credentials (auto-refresh)

```python
client = FoundryClient.from_oauth2(
    hostname="https://my-foundry.example.com",
    client_id="my-client-id",
    client_secret="my-client-secret",
    scopes="api:read-data api:write-data",
)
```

### Custom token provider

```python
from palantir_foundry.auth import TokenProvider

class MyVaultProvider(TokenProvider):
    def get_token(self) -> str:
        return vault.read("foundry/token")["data"]["value"]

from palantir_foundry import FoundryClient
client = FoundryClient(
    hostname="https://my-foundry.example.com",
    token_provider=MyVaultProvider(),
)
```

---

## Datasets API

```python
datasets = client.datasets

# Create a dataset
ds = datasets.create(
    name="my-new-dataset",
    parent_folder_rid="ri.compass.main.folder.abc",
)

# Open a transaction, upload a file, commit
txn = datasets.open_transaction(ds.rid, branch="master", transaction_type="APPEND")
datasets.upload_file(ds.rid, txn.rid, "/data/records.csv", b"id,name\n1,Alice\n")
datasets.commit_transaction(ds.rid, txn.rid)

# Read a file back
content = datasets.get_file_content(ds.rid, "/data/records.csv", branch="master")
print(content.decode())

# List all files (auto-paginated)
for file_info in datasets.list_files(ds.rid, branch="master"):
    print(file_info.path, file_info.size_bytes)

# Manage branches
branches = datasets.list_branches(ds.rid)
dev = datasets.create_branch(ds.rid, "dev", source_branch="master")
```

---

## Catalog API

```python
catalog = client.catalog

# Browse the resource tree
children = list(catalog.list_children("ri.compass.main.folder.root"))
for child in children:
    print(child.name, child.resource_type, child.rid)

# Resolve a path to a resource
resource = catalog.get_resource_by_path("/Projects/Analytics/my-dataset")

# Search
results = catalog.search_resources("sales data", resource_types=["dataset"])

# Create a folder
folder = catalog.create_folder("new-folder", parent_folder_rid="ri.compass.main.folder.root")
```

---

## Ontology API

```python
ontology = client.ontology

# Discover ontologies
for ont in ontology.list_ontologies():
    print(ont.api_name, ont.rid)

# List object types
types = ontology.list_object_types("ri.ontology.main.ontology.abc")

# Iterate all objects (auto-paginated)
for emp in ontology.list_objects(ont.rid, "Employee", order_by="lastName"):
    print(emp.primary_key, emp.properties)

# Fetch a single object
emp = ontology.get_object(ont.rid, "Employee", "EMP-001")

# Structured search
active = ontology.search_objects(
    ont.rid,
    "Employee",
    query={"type": "eq", "field": "status", "value": "active"},
    select=["id", "name", "department"],
)

# Apply an action
result = ontology.apply_action(
    ont.rid,
    "promoteEmployee",
    parameters={"employeeId": "EMP-001", "newTitle": "Senior Engineer"},
)
print(result.status)   # "SUCCESS"

# Execute a query function
output = ontology.execute_query(ont.rid, "headcountByDept", {"region": "EMEA"})
```

---

## Compass API

```python
compass = client.compass

# Upload a file within an open transaction
txn = client.datasets.open_transaction(ds_rid, branch="master")
compass.upload_file(
    dataset_rid=ds_rid,
    transaction_rid=txn.rid,
    logical_path="/reports/2024-Q1.pdf",
    content=open("report.pdf", "rb").read(),
    content_type="application/pdf",
)
client.datasets.commit_transaction(ds_rid, txn.rid)

# Download a file
pdf_bytes = compass.download_file(ds_rid, "/reports/2024-Q1.pdf", branch="master")

# File metadata
meta = compass.get_file_metadata(ds_rid, "/reports/2024-Q1.pdf")
print(meta.size_bytes, meta.content_type, meta.modified)

# List files with a prefix filter (auto-paginated)
for f in compass.list_files(ds_rid, branch="master", path_prefix="/reports/"):
    print(f.path)
```

---

## CLI Reference

Set credentials via environment variables:

```bash
export FOUNDRY_HOSTNAME=https://my-foundry.example.com
export FOUNDRY_TOKEN=my-api-token
```

Or pass them as flags:

```bash
palantir-foundry --hostname https://my-foundry.example.com --token my-token <command>
```

### Datasets commands

```bash
# Get dataset metadata
palantir-foundry datasets get ri.foundry.main.dataset.abc

# Create a dataset
palantir-foundry datasets create my-dataset ri.compass.main.folder.xyz

# List branches
palantir-foundry datasets list-branches ri.foundry.main.dataset.abc

# List files on a branch
palantir-foundry datasets list-files ri.foundry.main.dataset.abc --branch master

# Download a file (stdout or file)
palantir-foundry datasets download-file ri.foundry.main.dataset.abc /data/file.csv -o ./file.csv
```

### Catalog commands

```bash
# Get resource by RID
palantir-foundry catalog get ri.compass.main.folder.abc

# List children of a folder
palantir-foundry catalog ls ri.compass.main.folder.abc

# Search resources
palantir-foundry catalog search "sales report" --type dataset

# Create a folder
palantir-foundry catalog mkdir new-folder ri.compass.main.folder.abc
```

### Ontology commands

```bash
# List ontologies
palantir-foundry ontology list

# List object types
palantir-foundry ontology object-types ri.ontology.main.ontology.abc

# List objects (default 20)
palantir-foundry ontology objects ri.ontology.main.ontology.abc Employee --limit 50

# Apply an action
palantir-foundry ontology apply-action ri.ontology.main.ontology.abc createEmployee \
  '{"name": "Alice", "department": "Engineering"}'
```

---

## Error Handling

All API errors raise subclasses of `FoundryError`:

```python
from palantir_foundry.exceptions import (
    FoundryError,
    AuthenticationError,   # HTTP 401
    ForbiddenError,        # HTTP 403
    NotFoundError,         # HTTP 404
    ConflictError,         # HTTP 409
    RateLimitError,        # HTTP 429
    ServerError,           # HTTP 5xx
    ValidationError,       # HTTP 400
)

try:
    ds = client.datasets.get("ri.foundry.main.dataset.unknown")
except NotFoundError as e:
    print(f"Dataset not found: {e.message} (status={e.status_code})")
except RateLimitError:
    print("Rate limited — back off and retry")
except FoundryError as e:
    print(f"Foundry API error {e.status_code}: {e.message}")
```

